[32.4113, "o", "\u001b[29A\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Provider: anthropic-vertex\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Model: claude-opus-4-8\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Working directory: /tmp/ami-demo-fbt7wD\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Session: session-20261113-125452-857-0\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Permissions: auto-allow\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[90mTip: The AI can read, edit, and run code. Just ask.\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m\u2298 Indexing skipped: no project root found\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255m > Write a Python script called buffon.py that estimates \u03c0 using a Monte Carlo simulation of \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mBuffon's Needle problem. Drop 500,000 needles of length 1 onto a plane with parallel lines spaced 1 \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mapart, count how many cross a line, and compute the \u03c0 estimate as 2\u00b7N/crossings. Print a short \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255msummary table showing the number of needles, crossings, estimated \u03c0, true \u03c0, and the percentage \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255merror. Then run it with python3 buffon.py. \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[KI'll write the script and run it.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m[Checkpoint cp-1794570924597-1: /tmp/ami-demo-fbt7wD/buffon.py]\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u001b[38;5;167m\u25cf\u001b[39m \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;167mfile_edit\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\u001b[2m \u00b7 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;243m/tmp/ami-demo-fbt7wD/buffon.py\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;167m\u001b[39mfile_edit /tmp/ami-demo-fbt7wD/buffon.py \u001b[2m3.3s\u001b[22m\r\r\n